# What this repository must never carry — A64-030.2 (B-2).
#
# There was no `.gitignore` here at all, at any depth, and two files said
# otherwise: `infrastructure/production/production.env.example` claimed
# "`production.env` is gitignored", and `apps/api/.env.example` claimed
# "a file called `.env` is gitignored". Both were false, and `git
# check-ignore` matched nothing. The moment an operator filled in a real
# `production.env` on the production host, every secret on the platform was
# one `git add -A` from being published.
#
# The patterns below are this project's, not a template's: each line names
# an artefact this repository's own toolchain produces or a file its own
# documentation tells an operator to create.

# --- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Three shapes exist, so all three are refused: `.env`, `.env.<tier>` (which
# is what `app/config/environment.py` reads — `.env.local`), and
# `<tier>.env` (which is what `docker compose --env-file` takes —
# `production.env`, `staging.env`).
#
# The negation is last and is what keeps the four committed templates
# trackable. It is a suffix match rather than a list of paths so a new
# `*.env.example` beside a new tier does not need a line here.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!*.env.example

# Anything that is a key is a secret, whatever it is called. The
# certificate material this deployment uses lives in a Docker volume and in
# `/etc/letsencrypt` on the host, never here — these lines exist so that an
# operator who copies one into the checkout to look at it cannot commit it.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# --- Python — apps/api --------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/

# `StorageSettings.local_root` defaults to `var/storage`, resolved from the
# working directory — so running the API locally writes uploaded objects
# into `apps/api/var/`. A deployed tier uses S3 and never creates this.
apps/api/var/

# --- Node — apps/web, apps/admin ----------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright's defaults. `apps/web/playwright.config.ts` overrides neither.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# --- Operating system ---------------------------------------------------
#
# `.DS_Store` and `apps/.DS_Store` were tracked before this file existed.
.DS_Store
